# ~/.zshrc.local - your machine, your rules
# =============================================================================
#
# This file is YOURS. It is not managed by chezmoi, it is not part of the
# dotfiles-core repo, and `chezmoi apply` will never read, overwrite, or
# even look at it. Your ~/.zshrc (the one chezmoi manages) sources this
# file automatically near the top, so anything you put here takes effect
# in every new terminal.
#
# Use it for:
#   - work-specific tooling (VPNs, internal CLIs, company URLs)
#   - secrets or tokens (never put these in the shared, public repo!)
#   - personal aliases and shortcuts you don't want to share
#   - anything you're just trying out and don't want to commit to yet
#
# This file was copied here once, automatically, the first time chezmoi
# ran on this machine (see the run_once_after_90-seed-zshrc-local.sh
# script in dotfiles-core). It will NOT be touched again after that - edit
# it freely, nothing will overwrite it.
#
# Below are a few worked examples to get you started. They're all
# commented out - uncomment and edit the ones you want, or just delete
# them and write your own.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Example 1: a simple alias
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# alias gs="git status"

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Example 2: an environment variable / export
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# export MY_COMPANY_API_URL="https://api.example-work.com"

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Example 3: a function (put anything more than one line here)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# greet() {
#   echo "Hello, $1! It's $(date +'%A %H:%M')."
# }

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Example 4: something that only exists on THIS machine
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Guard machine-specific things with an existence check, so this file
# stays portable if you ever copy pieces of it to another Mac.
# if [[ -f "/Applications/SomeWorkTool.app/Contents/Resources/cli.sh" ]]; then
#   source "/Applications/SomeWorkTool.app/Contents/Resources/cli.sh"
# fi
